# What the Docker daemon must not send as build context.
#
# The Dockerfile needs only `requirements*.txt`, `app/` and `tools/`, but the
# context is the whole repository. Excluding the rest keeps the context small
# and — more importantly — keeps runtime state out of the image: a credential,
# a database or a log baked into a layer is readable by anyone who can pull the
# image, and survives every rotation.
#
# Two of these are load-bearing, not tidiness:
#   .env      — the bot token, the dashboard secret and every API key live here
#   data/     — the SQLite database and the runtime credential file
# Neither is copied by the Dockerfile today; this makes that a rule rather than
# an accident.

# Version control
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Python virtualenvs and caches
.venv
.venv-*
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Runtime state
data/
backups/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.log
logs/

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Not needed at build time
docs/
tests/
*.md
*.tar
*.tar.gz
